        <Variable.Default>
          <Literal x:TypeArguments="x:String">Extract all invoice information from the complete document. Return only information that is explicitly present in the document. Do not guess, calculate, infer, or invent values. For missing fields return an empty string. Extract EVERY invoice line item without skipping any rows. If the document contains an attached purchase order, distinguish the invoice information from the purchase order information. For invoice_lpo_po_number, always use the Order Number associated with the invoice because the Order Number is the LPO number. The Order Number may be present on the invoice or on an attached Purchase Order. If an attached Purchase Order contains an Order No., Order Number, or Order # that corresponds to the invoice, use that value. Never use the Invoice Number as invoice_lpo_po_number. For invoice_due_date, only return a date if an explicit due date is present. For Invoice To extract the associated with fields names like Customer Name, To, Customer, this corresponds to the invoice_to use that value never use address in place of it. Extract Summery from the Purchase Order document which is attached with in the document, extract full summary if it is multi or single line where the subheading will be as summary. Do not derive a due date from payment terms such as 30 Net. Return the data according to the provided JSON schema.</Literal>
        </Variable.Default>
      </Variable>
